  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam-Netherlands WaterTech Challenge 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam faces many challenges in managing its water resources, including water pollution, water scarcity, irrigation inefficiencies, climate change, and lack of infrastructure. The growth in industry and agriculture has put significant pressure on water resources, with industrial activities expected to account for over 45% of national GDP by 2010.Involving and activating the younger generation in Vietnam could help address these water-related problems, and proposes a water innovation challenge for start-ups and graduates in Vietnam to develop solutions. The priority sectors for this project are agriculture and industry, which face unique challenges related to water.The project could also provide a platform for start-ups and graduates to connect with potential investors, customers, and partners. Overall, addressing these challenges will require a concerted effort from government, industry, and civil society to improve water management practices, invest in infrastructure, and promote sustainable water use.</narrative>
  </description>
